### InverSeek Ingestion Service - runnable HTTP checks
### Open in IntelliJ (HTTP Client) or VS Code (REST Client). Expected results are in the comments.

@base = http://localhost:7001

### 1. Health -> 200 {"service":"ingestion","status":"UP",...}
GET {{base}}/health

### 2. Ingest a new book -> 200 {"status":"downloaded","path":"AAAAMMDD/HH/1342",...}
POST {{base}}/ingest/1342

### 3. Same book again (idempotent) -> 200 {"status":"available"}, same path, no new download
POST {{base}}/ingest/1342

### 4. Status of a downloaded book -> 200 {"status":"available"}
GET {{base}}/ingest/status/1342

### 5. Status of a book never ingested -> 404 {"status":"not_available"}
GET {{base}}/ingest/status/11

### 6. List downloaded books -> 200 {"count":N,"books":[...]} in ascending order
GET {{base}}/ingest/list

### 7. Invalid id -> 400 {"error":"invalid_book_id"}
POST {{base}}/ingest/abc

### 8. Book that does not exist on Gutenberg -> 404 {"error":"book_not_found"}
POST {{base}}/ingest/9999999
